<!--
  TEST RIDERS for the Animalia elk and moose (#646, docs/features/animalia-elk-moose.md), 2026-09-23.

  Two clones of mirkwood_rochenlas (its committed kit, skills and face) that ride the new horse-skeleton
  reskins, so their retargeted clips can be watched in a Custom Battle:
      taom.spawn_troops taom_test_animalia_elk_rider 5 ally
      taom.spawn_troops taom_test_animalia_moose_rider 5 enemy
  Registered for CustomGame ONLY (Main/_Module/SubModule.xml), so no campaign, save or culture roster ever
  sees them; nothing upgrades into or out of them. Remove this file, its SubModule block and both riders'
  exemptions (tools/taom_schema.py _ARMOUR_LADDER_EXEMPT, tools/melee_ladders.json exempt_troops: a stale
  exemption is itself a finding) before the next player release (Mike, 2026-09-23: keep them visible until
  then; the Custom Battle picker lists them). Since the riders were reassigned, mirkwood_rochenlas rides the
  Animalia elk, so the elk rider duplicates it; only heroes ride the moose, so the moose rider is still the
  one troop that spawns on one. The exemptions keep this file from being counted as a kingdom.

  Every Horse slot carries a harness (MOUNT_WITHOUT_HARNESS): the Animalia meshes are bare animals, and
  taom_elk_saddle_a (the great elk's saddle, #636) is the seat until they get their own.
-->

